      "message": "I see why this is useful for making `REQUEUE` explicit in the logs, but I\u0027m not sure it belongs in BrokerApi.\n\nFrom the transport side, `send()` and `requeue()` do the same thing: publish an Event to a topic.\n\nWhat makes it a requeue is the client\u0027s intention: for example, `multi-site` decided to retry a failed event. From a transport-layer perspective, though, I don\u0027t see a real difference between the two operations.\n\nTo me, `BrokerApi` should expose the broker operations, such as sending and receiving messages. Requeuing is not something this API can actually do; it is how a client chooses to use `send()` after handling a failed event.\n\nWDYT?",
